#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""rota — manage Claude accounts and show Claude + Codex subscription usage.

Commands:
  rota                     Usage bars for all Claude and Codex subscriptions
  rota usage [name]        Usage for one Claude account, or all subscriptions
  rota switch [email]      Switch accounts (prefix ok: `rota switch dev`);
                           with no email, switch to the best account
  rota add [email]         Enroll a new account via an in-process browser login
                           (never touches the live login; does not switch)
  rota reauth <email>      Re-authenticate a saved account whose refresh token
                           expired, in place — no switching, no logout.
                           `--all` walks every dead account; add --manual when
                           a browser can't reach localhost.
  rota list                List accounts with token health (active one marked)
  rota whoami              Show the active account
  rota export [email...]   Print account snapshots as JSON (contains secrets!)
  rota import <file|->     Import snapshots exported on another machine
  rota remove <email>      Delete an account snapshot
  rota save                Repair: re-snapshot the live login (rarely needed)

Codex commands (independent of the Claude account — switching one never
touches the other):
  rota codex               Usage for all Codex subscriptions
  rota codex switch [name] Switch the active Codex account; with no name,
                           switch to the account with the most headroom
  rota codex add           Enroll a new Codex account via `codex login`
                           (does not switch)
  rota codex list          List saved Codex accounts
  rota codex save [name]   Snapshot the live Codex login
  rota codex remove <name> Delete a Codex account snapshot
  rota codex whoami        Show the active Codex account

Notes:
  - Snapshots live in ~/.claude/accounts/<name>.json (chmod 600).
  - Switching swaps only the claudeAiOauth key in .credentials.json, so MCP
    server OAuth (Sentry/Notion/Linear/...) is untouched.
  - Codex snapshots live in $CODEX_HOME/accounts/<name>/auth.json; switching
    swaps only $CODEX_HOME/auth.json, so Codex config/history stay shared and
    the Claude login is never touched.
  - Refresh tokens are single-use (rotated on refresh) and their lifetime is
    fixed at login (~60 days) — refreshing does not extend it. rota refreshes
    when an access token is expired or a request 401s, and writes rotated
    tokens back to both the snapshot and the live file. Once a refresh token
    is rejected the account is marked dead and left alone (no more requests,
    so no 429 lockouts) until `rota reauth <email>`.
  - Usage results are cached in ~/.claude/accounts/.usage-cache.json; when a
    fetch fails (rate limit, network) the last good numbers are shown, marked
    with their age.
  - Avoid switching while another Claude Code session is mid-conversation;
    running sessions keep their old identity.
"""

